Largest subarray with 0 sum
Given an array arr[] containing both positive and negative integers, the task is to find the length of the longest subarray with a sum equals to 0.

Explanation:
In this qustion we need to find the longest subarray where sum==0. Same - just sotre prefix sum initally fr elements... 
but store unique prefixSum cause we only want the first occurance to count the largest length.
after that reset prefix sum.
again start iterating and saving prefixsum, 
check if right away the prefixSum==0, then maxLength=i+1.
again with if condition check if map contains prefixSum that was just calculated
(THis is just because suppose if prefix sum repeats itself, then subarray sum is 0
{15 -2 2} - consider this array... Prefix sum is {15, 13, 15}... here prefixSum is not 0, but {-2,2} has subbary sum 0...
we also notice that subbary sum repeats itself 15->15...So length -> 2-0 = 2.... so longest subarray Length =2 
)
, then calculate the longestLength based on the index

Code:

class Solution {
    int maxLength(int arr[]) {
        // code here
        HashMap<Integer,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        int prefixSum=0; 
        int n = arr.length;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            prefixSum+=arr[i];
            if(!map.containsKey(prefixSum)){
                map.put(prefixSum,i);
            }
        }
        
        prefixSum=0; int longestLength = 0;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            prefixSum+=arr[i];
            // Case 1: Prefix Sum itself is 0
            if(prefixSum==0){
                longestLength = Math.max(longestLength, i+1);
            }
            // Case 2: Prefix Sum repeats itself - then still it shows subarray with sum 0
            if(map.containsKey(prefixSum)){
                int firstIndex = map.get(prefixSum);
                int length = i- firstIndex;
                longestLength = Math.max(longestLength, length);
            }
        }
        
        return longestLength;
    }
}
